# --- Worked-example cases (data + produced artifacts; NOT in the package) --
# Each case lives under cases/<name>/ and keeps ONLY its case-config.yml, the
# example scripts (*.py) and docs (*.md) in version control. The large source
# data go in cases/<name>/user-sources/ and the produced artifacts in
# cases/<name>/hydromate-case/ (preprocessing/ simulation/ postprocessing/
# calibration-validation/) - both kept out of git (well over the 20 MB push limit).
# ignore all case user-sources contents (real data), but keep the template's
# README that documents the expected data layout.
/cases/*/user-sources/**
!/cases/case-template/user-sources/README.md
/cases/*/hydromate-case/
/cases/*/tm-simulation/
/projection.info

# --- Build outputs / generated TELEMAC cases -------------------------------
hydromate-case/
tm-simulation/
case/
*.slf
*.log

# --- Heavy / geospatial / tabular data (safety net for the 20 MB limit) -----
# Belt-and-suspenders so large binaries never get committed even outside the
# case folders above. The CI workflow (.github/workflows/file-size-limit.yml)
# additionally fails any push/PR carrying a tracked file larger than 20 MB.
*.tif
*.tiff
*.tfw
*.gpkg
*.gpkg-shm
*.gpkg-wal
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.cpg
*.sbn
*.sbx
*.qgz
*.qgs
*.xlsx
*.las
*.laz

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg

# --- Environments / editors / tooling --------------------------------------
.venv/
.env
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
.spyproject/
# emacs autosave / backup files, which otherwise sit next to an edited config and
# get swept into a commit (#case-config.yml#, case-config.yml~)
\#*\#
.\#*
*~

# --- Generated case status markers ---------------------------------------
# MODEL=<SOLVER>_<ENABLED|DISABLED> reports the CURRENTLY available setup: whether
# the solver environment resolves on this machine and how far this working tree has
# got. That is local state, like hydromate-case/ - a tracked copy would churn on
# every build and would be a confident lie in a fresh clone. Regenerated by every
# build and by `hydromate status`. The case-template keeps a committed example.
cases/*/MODEL=*
!cases/case-template/MODEL=*

# --- OpenFOAM cases ------------------------------------------------------
# Generated cases live under the already-ignored cases/*/hydromate-case/; this is
# the safety net for a case built anywhere else. A polyMesh alone runs to hundreds
# of MB and the per-processor copies multiply it by the core count.
processor*/
constant/polyMesh/
*.foam
postProcessing/

# --- Sphinx docs build ---
docs/_build/

# --- Local backup tooling ---------------------------------------------------
/scripts/backup-logs/

# --- build outputs ---------------------------------------------------------
# The QGIS plugin zip is built from a tag by CI (and reproducibly by
# scripts/build_plugin_zip.py); it is a release asset, not source.
/dist/
docs/_build/
